# Direct dependencies, with the ranges a human reviews.
#
# requirements.txt holds the exact resolved set actually used and verified.
# Regenerate it deliberately, review the diff, and re-run the test suite:
#
#   python -m venv /tmp/caspel-resolve
#   /tmp/caspel-resolve/bin/pip install -r requirements.in
#   /tmp/caspel-resolve/bin/pip freeze | sort > requirements.txt
#
# The image installs requirements.txt, never requirements.in, so an image
# rebuilt six months from now gets the same packages it was tested against
# instead of whatever is newest that day.

